WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.217
Let’s start with variables. A variable is simply a meaningful name connected to a value.

00:00:06.217 --> 00:00:13.147
If a company has one thousand dollars in sales, we can store that value in a variable named sales.

00:00:13.147 --> 00:00:15.672
We can do the same with costs.

00:00:15.672 --> 00:00:23.662
Once those values have names, a formula such as sales minus costs is much easier to understand than a formula made only

00:00:23.662 --> 00:00:25.444
of numbers.

00:00:25.894 --> 00:00:28.546
Good variable names communicate meaning.

00:00:28.546 --> 00:00:35.336
Names like monthly_sales, patient_age, or total_cost tell the reader what the data represents.

00:00:35.336 --> 00:00:43.121
A vague name like x may work, but it makes the code harder to read.

00:00:43.121 --> 00:00:46.416
Variables also make code reusable.

00:00:46.416 --> 00:00:50.046
Change the value, and the same calculation can run again.
